val22=le point \($(val11[4])\) se superpose au point <span class="nowrap">\($(val11[1])\),</span>	              <p>le point \($(val11[5])\) se superpose au point <span class="nowrap">\($(val11[2])\),</span></p>	              le point \($(val11[6])\) se superpose au point <span class="nowrap">\($(val11[3])\),</span>	              <p>donc, par la symétrie d'axe <span class="nowrap">\(($(val8[1]))\),</span> l'image du triangle \($(val11[4])$(val11[5])$(val11[6])\)	              est <span class="nowrap">\($(val11[1])$(val11[2])$(val11[3])\).</span></p>
!if $val6=it 
